WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:09.120
The FDA has authorized the Pfizer Bion tech&nbsp;
coronavirus vaccine. They did it on Friday night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:15.760
Now, it came under a cloud of allegations that&nbsp;
either Trump or his chief of staff, Mark Meadows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:22.800
or someone called the FDA director, Steven Hahn,&nbsp;
and said approve this today. And when Steven Hahn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.880
was interviewed about that over the weekend, he&nbsp;
didn't deny it. He just insisted everything was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.720
done based on the science. And to me, that's&nbsp;
a pretty clear nondenial. But the point is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.240
we now have an approved vaccine. The same&nbsp;
vaccine has been approved in the U.K.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.480
It has been approved in Canada, and now it&nbsp;
has been approved here in the United States.&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.480
Vaccination starts today, as far as we&nbsp;
know, with high risk health care workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.200
believed to be getting top priority in all 50&nbsp;
states. Ultimately, states decide how to allocate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.040
and prioritize the tranches of doses that they&nbsp;
will be receiving. We have three million doses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.800
already fanning out across the country via&nbsp;
logistics and shipping companies over the weekend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.360
One hundred and forty five different&nbsp;
sites will be receiving the vaccine today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:18.800
Another four hundred sites tomorrow, another sixty&nbsp;
something on Wednesday. Now, there is not nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:25.360
enough supply. Even if now we say we're just doing&nbsp;
medical workers, we don't yet have the supply to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.600
inoculate every doctor, nurse, hospital, security&nbsp;
guard, receptionist, phlebotomist, other workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.440
who risk being exposed every single&nbsp;
day. We just don't have enough doses yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.680
because the vaccines can cause side effects&nbsp;
like fevers and aches for a day or two.&nbsp;

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.680
Hospitals also can't even if they had all the&nbsp;
doses, they can't give it to everybody at once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.240
because everybody might be out sick the next day.&nbsp;
Obviously, it's only a fraction that actually get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:55.280
the side effects, but you have to stagger it&nbsp;
in order to avoid even the possibility of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:01.200
So this is going to be a process. Residents of&nbsp;
nursing homes who have been disproportionately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.160
suffering the death by coronavirus&nbsp;
are also expected to be top priority.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.800
And again, this is all based on expected shipping.&nbsp;
We're expecting to see some nursing home residents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.800
start to be vaccinated next week. New York's&nbsp;
first coronavirus vaccines have arrived and we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:26.160
expecting vaccinations today at Long Island Jewish&nbsp;
Medical Center and maybe even a couple of other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.800
locations. Most people's eligibility based&nbsp;
on prioritization is likely to put them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.960
sometime around spring for being able to get&nbsp;
a vaccine. The New York Times reported that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:45.200
the administration had a plan to vaccinate all&nbsp;
of its own staff, including people that work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.120
around Trump, even though these first doses&nbsp;
are supposed to go to health care workers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.840
And apparently there was not good reaction to&nbsp;
that. Donald Trump canceling that by Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.880
yesterday, saying, quote, People working in&nbsp;
the White House should receive the vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.880
somewhat later in the program, unless specifically&nbsp;
necessary. I have asked that this adjustment be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:10.080
made. I am not scheduled to take the vaccine, but&nbsp;
look forward to doing so at the appropriate time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:16.800
Still, we are going to have to deal with vaccine&nbsp;
hesitancy issues among some, and that's raising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:22.880
questions about whether all available doses will&nbsp;
even be requested once we get my expectation is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.920
now, with the doses going to health care workers&nbsp;
and still not having enough for all of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.200
every dose will be spoken for. For now in the&nbsp;
nursing home phase, I believe every dose will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:39.360
be spoken for once we get a second approved&nbsp;
vaccine. Moderna more than likely and we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.200
the next layer, which is likely going to be the&nbsp;
old folks if you don't have the demand that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.880
expect. And as of right now, sixty percent&nbsp;
of the country plans to get the vaccine, 40&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:04:00.240
percent of the country does not. You could have a&nbsp;
situation where even these early batches of doses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:07.520
don't get swept up. And in that case,&nbsp;
there's going to be some real questions. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:14.400
you know, the the idea would be that over time,&nbsp;
as you start to see, oh, my kids school requires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.120
that parents to be vaccinated, I don't know if&nbsp;
that's possible or eventually if the vaccines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.880
are open for kids, the kid to be vaccinated or&nbsp;
if I want to fly with this airline, I have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.720
be vaccinated. I want to go to a sporting event.&nbsp;
I have to be vaccinated. That will probably push&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.920
the number of people wanting the vaccine up from&nbsp;
sixty. They will call it a mandatory vaccination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:38.080
Of course it won't be. It will be if you want to&nbsp;
partake in a certain service or business. Then you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:43.360
have to choose to go and get a vaccine. It's up&nbsp;
to you ultimately, but we could have a situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:50.560
where because of under use of the vaccines, due to&nbsp;
lack of interest, you're going to have a situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.160
where people may well be able to jump the line.&nbsp;
And what I mean by that is if hospitals are giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:01.040
the vaccines to their workers, they know who&nbsp;
qualifies. If nursing homes or homes are giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:07.040
vaccines to their residents, they know these are&nbsp;
our residents. Once you get beyond that, from what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:12.320
I've been reading, CVS and Walgreens aren't&nbsp;
going to check. Do you really have diabetes?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.800
Is that do you actually qualify right now under&nbsp;
the you have to have one or two comorbidities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.040
And so the opportunity to jump the line is&nbsp;
likely to be a real thing. Now, at the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:29.040
if not everybody wants the vaccine, you may have&nbsp;
doses left over. And I don't know how it's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:35.600
to be chaotic to some degree. My approach is going&nbsp;
to be at no point will I act in a way where I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.240
taking a vaccine away from someone who's higher&nbsp;
priority than me, who wants it. If it becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.280
clear that the doses are not actually being&nbsp;
swept up by the people who are next on the list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.800
and there's an announcement of come and get&nbsp;
one or pay a hundred bucks and come and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:58.960
one because we have doses unclaimed that will go&nbsp;
bad if somebody doesn't get vaccinated. I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.920
absolutely do that. But I have no interest in&nbsp;
jumping the line if it's going to actually take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:09.600
vaccine away from someone who is up next in terms&nbsp;
of the vaccination protocol, that's my mindset.&nbsp;

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.000
And we're going to take it a week at a time&nbsp;
and track the number of people who have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.600
vaccinated, remembering that you are not&nbsp;
considered sort of a maximum inoculation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:24.640
until seven days after dose number two.&nbsp;
Very, very important to remember that.&nbsp;

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:29.520
Let me know where your head is on&nbsp;
vaccination. I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.760
We'll take a quick break and continue with more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:34.164
right after The David Pakman&nbsp;
Show at David Pakman Dotcom.

